title: Ray Anderson
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Founder of the carpet tile company [[Interface|Interface Flooring]]. 1934–2011.

In 1994 a customer asked what his company was doing for the environment, and he had no answer. He read Paul Hawken's //The Ecology of Commerce// and called it a "spear in the chest."

Then he stood up in front of his own staff and called himself a "plunderer" of the earth.

He spent the rest of his life trying to make a carpet company that takes nothing it can't give back.

See [[Does a sign become more honest when its maker admits what it doesn't yet do?]], [[Circular Economy]], [[Technical Nutrient]]

